            "text": "Yes \u2014 **early Coca-Cola did contain coca leaf extract**, and coca leaves naturally contain **cocaine alkaloids**.\n\nKey points:\n\n- Coca-Cola was invented in **1886** by John Pemberton.\n- The original formula used **extract of coca leaves** and **kola nuts** \u2014 hence \u201cCoca-Cola.\u201d\n- At the time, cocaine was legal and commonly used in patent medicines.\n- Around the early **1900s**, Coca-Cola began removing cocaine from the drink.\n- Since about **1903**, Coca-Cola has used **\u201cspent\u201d coca leaves**, meaning leaves processed to remove cocaine.\n- Modern Coca-Cola **does not contain cocaine**.\n\nSo the short answer is: **historically, yes; today, no.**",
